# Per-machine Claude Code state — settings.local.json, worktrees, whatever a session leaves.
# The contents are ignored rather than the directory, so that skills/ can be excepted: git
# does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, and a negation inside one never matches.
.claude/*
# …except the skills, which are shared work: a skill is instructions for driving this repo,
# and one that lives on a single laptop is one nobody else can use.
!.claude/skills/
.worktrees/
/verse
/o
/sourced
dist/
# mkdocs build output (`mkdocs build` defaults here; `mkdocs serve` needs nothing)
site/
# fetched on demand by scripts/check-mermaid.sh, at whatever version the site loads
scripts/mermaid/node_modules/
# working space inside the repo: probes, one-off harnesses, throwaway mains.
# In-tree so a Go file there can import the module; ignored so none of it is a commit.
scratchpad/
